WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:03.582
Building an AI-assisted scientific
workflow

2
00:00:03.582 --> 00:00:05.643
starts with a practical choice:

3
00:00:05.863 --> 00:00:07.224
where will the tools run?

4
00:00:07.324 --> 00:00:08.165
For this course,

5
00:00:08.685 --> 00:00:10.766
our foundation is Ubuntu Linux.

6
00:00:11.547 --> 00:00:12.909
For scientific computing,

7
00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:14.332
Ubuntu gives us access

8
00:00:14.332 --> 00:00:16.415
to an open-source software ecosystem.

9
00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:18.419
We can combine numerical solvers,

10
00:00:18.579 --> 00:00:20.743
physics libraries, automation scripts,

11
00:00:20.763 --> 00:00:22.766
and AI agents in one workflow.

12
00:00:23.447 --> 00:00:25.189
The same Linux-based approach

13
00:00:25.209 --> 00:00:26.530
also connects naturally

14
00:00:26.731 --> 00:00:28.072
to laboratory servers

15
00:00:28.112 --> 00:00:30.254
and high-performance computing clusters.

16
00:00:30.475 --> 00:00:32.577
The software and resource requirements

17
00:00:32.897 --> 00:00:35.020
still depend on the calculation.

18
00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:36.901
But you do not need

19
00:00:36.901 --> 00:00:39.402
a dedicated Linux computer to begin.

20
00:00:39.482 --> 00:00:41.663
On a compatible Windows 11 computer,

21
00:00:41.883 --> 00:00:45.845
Ubuntu on WSL 2 provides a Linux
environment

22
00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:47.986
alongside your existing Windows setup.

23
00:00:48.647 --> 00:00:50.408
That is the setup we will use

24
00:00:50.408 --> 00:00:51.428
in these tutorials:

25
00:00:51.809 --> 00:00:55.070
Windows 11, WSL 2, and Ubuntu.

26
00:00:55.471 --> 00:00:56.451
It lets us work

27
00:00:56.451 --> 00:00:58.372
with Linux-based scientific tools

28
00:00:58.632 --> 00:01:01.293
while keeping our familiar Windows
applications.

29
00:01:01.973 --> 00:01:03.574
The key message is simple.

30
00:01:04.034 --> 00:01:06.236
Start with the computer you already have.

31
00:01:06.716 --> 00:01:08.677
Build a consistent environment,

32
00:01:08.897 --> 00:01:09.938
connect the tools,

33
00:01:10.238 --> 00:01:12.279
and focus on the scientific workflow.

34
00:01:13.999 --> 00:01:17.979
Let's make OpenCode part of your scientific workflow.

35
00:01:19.159 --> 00:01:21.919
OpenCode is an AI coding assistant.

36
00:01:22.359 --> 00:01:26.199
Start at opencode.ai.download where you find

37
00:01:26.199 --> 00:01:27.899
